From 22a5e87cc51aa83be550abe1c17e0b4203f18c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:20:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Headless and embedded aarch64 support

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Driving the engine without a desktop:
- skip the launcher window when a game folder is given, or on --no-launcher
- report caught exceptions to stderr as well as the modal error window, which
  otherwise spins at 100% CPU with nobody to close it
- stream the engine log in headless mode, so LogUnimplemented() is visible
- return non-zero after a caught exception

Cross-compiling for an embedded aarch64 target:
- ENABLE_X11 / ENABLE_WAYLAND options, so an SDL2-only build can configure
  against a sysroot with no X11, no compositor and no desktop GL
- missing <cstring>/<cmath> in the SDL2 backend, rarely built on Linux
- link SDL from pkg-config: the link used SDL2_LIBRARY, which find_package sets
  and pkg_search_module does not
- ZIPDIR_EXECUTABLE, since zipdir runs on the build machine
- system fonts without GSettings or fontconfig

Rationale for each is in port/engine-patches/README.md.
